{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1UEHXYh18NviAANDxo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Make the fix now. Don't hold it back for a survey.**\n\n**Why the survey shouldn't block it**\n- You already have direct evidence of the problem. 18% of searches return nothing, the top zero-result terms are mostly part numbers with formatting differences, and about 340 calls a month are tagged \"can't find part online\". A satisfaction survey only measures how people feel about it, which is weaker evidence.\n- A survey would take weeks and would likely miss the people with the worst experience. Customers who gave up and phoned in, or went to a competitor, are the least likely to reply.\n- The cost is small and easy to undo. Three days of engineering is cheap next to 340 calls a month of sales time, plus the orders you lose without ever seeing them.\n\n**Check before building (about an hour)**\nRun the top 200 zero-result terms against the catalogue with dashes and spaces stripped, offline. This shows how many would actually match. If many are supplier numbers your catalogue doesn't contain at all, you need a supplier-to-SKU cross-reference table, not just normalisation. That changes the scope, so find out before committing the three days.\n\n**Measure the result**\n- Before release, record the current zero-result rate, the hit rate on those top 200 terms, the monthly count of \"can't find part\" calls, and search-to-order conversion.\n- After release, compare the same numbers over 4–6 weeks. A drop in calls is the result your head of sales will care about most.\n\n**What to say to your head of sales**\nA survey is still worth running, but in parallel and aimed at what the logs can't show: filters, product data quality, and how customers prefer to search. Running it after the fix also gives them a cleaner baseline, because it will pick up the next problem instead of one you've already found."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3189,"cache_read_input_tokens":5035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3189},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2219eb96-ed72-445e-94aa-ae13e548b6f5","uuid":"2025d9ec-600f-4b9d-aea4-573bc83bf59d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:12:38.817Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1UDzvWLSCEm5r9LHqc"}
